        "original_id": "d57e8fbe-6d4a-54ed-8849-7060912562e4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Public Television 19, Inc.\n- Television stations: KCPT, KCTV\n- Radio stations: KTBG\n- Television programs: Check, Please!\n- People: Wendall Anschutz\n- Places: Kansas City, Missouri; Kansas City, Kansas; Union Hill; Blue Valley; East 31st Street; 23rd Street and Stark Avenue\n\nFacts:\n- KCTV is a CBS-affiliated television station licensed to Kansas City, Missouri, and it also serves Kansas City, Kansas.\n- Wendall Anschutz was born on January 21, 1938.\n- Wendall Anschutz was a television newsman for KCTV in Kansas City, Missouri, from 1966 until his retirement in 2001.\n- Check, Please! began airing on KCPT in Kansas City in 2009.\n- Wendall Anschutz died on January 7, 2010.\n- KCPT is owned by Public Television 19, Inc.\n- KCPT maintains studio facilities on East 31st Street in Kansas City, Missouri's Union Hill section, and those facilities are shared with sister radio station KTBG (90.9 FM).\n- KCPT's studio facilities are adjacent to the transmitter tower of KCTV.\n- KCPT's transmitter is located near 23rd Street and Stark Avenue in Kansas City, Missouri's Blue Valley section.",
